            <div xml:id="d680">

                <pb facs="0798" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13114: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-06T17:00:00+08:00">June 6, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 6—2:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>245. Legation’s 226, May 29, 4 p.m.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d680-f1"/> Vice Consul
                    at Yunnanfu reports as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 5, 3 p.m. Reds captured Luting on June 1st and Tatsienlu on the
                            3rd. No information has been received concerning American citizens
                            resident at the latter place.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
